WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.227 --> 00:00:17.601
The scrimmage against the Swallows was an away game.

2
00:00:17.602 --> 00:00:23.495
"I'm ready," Patrick repeated under his breath. But he hadn't gotten much sleep the night before.

3
00:00:23.496 --> 00:00:28.871
His math quiz with a red 57 had sat on his desk like a warning light.

4
00:00:28.872 --> 00:00:32.258
And he'd been worried about who would start as catcher today.

5
00:00:32.259 --> 00:00:38.559
Patrick rubbed his lucky catcher's mitt as Coach slapped the roster on the dugout wall.

6
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:42.029
"Here's the lineup, boys. Ready to play baseball?"

7
00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:44.509
"Yeah!" roared the team.

8
00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:50.723
Patrick took a deep breath and went over to look at the roster.

9
00:00:50.724 --> 00:00:54.807
Second up for bat, Patrick Deboe, Number 12.

10
00:00:54.808 --> 00:01:01.034
Dell flashed him a grin. "Mickey's good. But you and I have got the dance down."

11
00:01:01.035 --> 00:01:02.848
Patrick grinned too.

12
00:01:02.848 --> 00:01:10.289
He and Dell were good dance partners, meaning that as pitcher and catcher, they could follow each other's moves instinctively.

13
00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:15.891
"Play ball!" the umpire yelled a few minutes later.

14
00:01:15.892 --> 00:01:22.462
The Dragons were up first. Patrick managed to hit a single.

15
00:01:22.463 --> 00:01:26.705
But the next three batters struck out, so the Dragons went scoreless.

16
00:01:26.706 --> 00:01:34.356
Dell headed to the mound while Patrick took his position behind home plate.

17
00:01:34.357 --> 00:01:42.593
"First game. First pitch," he thought happily. Mickey was a nice guy, but beating him for the starter position sure felt sweet.

18
00:01:42.594 --> 00:01:46.250
Now he had to prove he deserved to keep the position.

19
00:01:46.251 --> 00:01:49.679
The first batter up for the other team was Number 14.

20
00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:53.845
Patrick remembered that this batter was the one who crowded the plate.

21
00:01:53.846 --> 00:02:01.658
Patrick put down one finger to signal a fast pitch. Dell wound up and whizzed it in.

22
00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:04.513
"Strike!" called the umpire.

23
00:02:04.514 --> 00:02:10.925
Patrick nodded at Dell. Two more pitches, two more strikes, and they had their first out.

24
00:02:10.926 --> 00:02:13.848
"Nice work, you two!" called Daniel.

25
00:02:13.849 --> 00:02:17.662
"Finally, a compliment from Daniel!" Patrick thought.

26
00:02:17.663 --> 00:02:24.240
Number 42 tapped his cleats with the bat and planted his feet in the dirt.

27
00:02:24.241 --> 00:02:31.238
Patrick remembered that this kid was a good hitter. He put down two fingers to signal a curve ball to Dell.

28
00:02:31.239 --> 00:02:33.206
Swoosh.

29
00:02:33.207 --> 00:02:34.872
"Strike!"

30
00:02:34.873 --> 00:02:41.639
The batter caught a piece of the next pitch, but the ball went foul. Patrick caught it easily.

31
00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:45.805
Patrick grinned. They had two outs already.

32
00:02:45.806 --> 00:02:49.579
In middle school baseball, the teams played seven innings.

33
00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:54.209
By the bottom of the final inning, the Dragons were ahead, 7-6.

34
00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:57.272
Number 42 for the Swallows was up again.

35
00:02:57.274 --> 00:03:01.470
"He looks ready to slam a homerun," thought Patrick.

36
00:03:01.471 --> 00:03:03.669
He signaled Dell for the changeup.

37
00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:09.120
Dell's pitch was high, but Number 42 hit it solidly.

38
00:03:09.121 --> 00:03:17.353
The ball sailed just inside third base. In left field Todd dove for it.

39
00:03:17.354 --> 00:03:24.162
Patrick held his breath as Todd rolled on the field. Would Todd come up with it?

40
00:03:24.163 --> 00:03:30.122
"Yes!" screamed Patrick, seeing Todd's glove firmly wrapped around the ball.

41
00:03:30.123 --> 00:03:34.261
Two outs! One more out and the Dragons would win!

42
00:03:34.262 --> 00:03:39.809
Then everyone got quiet—Todd was still lying on the field.

43
00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:43.159
"Oh no," Patrick thought.

44
00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:47.769
Coach jogged out to check Todd's injury.

45
00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:54.661
Minutes later Todd stood, gingerly holding his arm against his chest.

46
00:03:54.662 --> 00:04:01.883
The crowd clapped as he walked off the field with Coach and over to his parents.

47
00:04:01.884 --> 00:04:07.414
Coach hurried over to the dugout and motioned for Mickey. Then he looked at Patrick.

48
00:04:07.415 --> 00:04:15.080
"Take left field, Patrick. This next batter hits deep, so we need someone with experience. Mickey will go in as catcher."

49
00:04:15.081 --> 00:04:22.312
"Okay, Coach," Patrick mumbled. He pulled off his catcher equipment and found his glove.

50
00:04:22.313 --> 00:04:26.221
As he put on his cap, he glanced at the Swallows' next batter.

51
00:04:26.222 --> 00:04:30.149
This kid liked the pitches low. Should he warn Mickey?

52
00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:34.293
"Nah. That's Daniel's job," thought Patrick.

53
00:04:34.294 --> 00:04:40.789
Dell's first pitch was a strike. Then a wild pitch from Dell put the Swallows batter on base.

54
00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:48.448
"That wasn't Mickey's fault," Patrick thought. But still the catcher always took the blame. It was just part of the job.

55
00:04:48.449 --> 00:04:52.876
The next batter had a chance to bring in the runner and tie up the score.

56
00:04:52.877 --> 00:04:59.295
Dell sent the pitch in, low and outside. The batter swung.

57
00:04:59.296 --> 00:05:07.120
The ball popped up behind home plate. Mickey scrambled to catch it, pulling off his mask.

58
00:05:07.121 --> 00:05:12.261
The ball drifted near the fence and then fell down, down . . .

59
00:05:12.262 --> 00:05:20.014
Mickey stretched over the fence, teetering to keep his balance. The ball settled solidly into his mitt.

60
00:05:20.015 --> 00:05:25.243
"Out!" cried the umpire. "Game over!"

61
00:05:25.244 --> 00:05:32.234
The Dragons had won! The team swarmed around home plate to congratulate Mickey.

62
00:05:32.235 --> 00:05:36.675
"What an amazing catch!" Patrick clapped Mickey on the back.

63
00:05:36.676 --> 00:05:42.403
"Thanks." Mickey grinned. "Another inch outside the fence and I wouldn't have reached it."

64
00:05:42.404 --> 00:05:48.481
The two of them joined the line to shake hands with the other team.

65
00:05:48.482 --> 00:05:54.242
Patrick tapped the hand of the Swallows player who had made the last out, feeling sorry for the guy.

66
00:05:54.243 --> 00:05:57.409
It was bad luck to be the hitter who made the last out.

67
00:05:57.410 --> 00:06:01.481
In the dugout everyone kept raving about Mickey's catch.

68
00:06:01.482 --> 00:06:07.145
Patrick was glad his team had won, but he felt a little jealous that he had missed the main action.

69
00:06:07.146 --> 00:06:14.977
"It's just one game," he told himself. "Next time you'll be back where you belong—behind home plate."

70
00:06:14.978 --> 00:06:18.308
"Huh?" Patrick said the next morning at school.

71
00:06:18.309 --> 00:06:24.791
Dell repeated the bad news. "Todd injured his shoulder. He's out for at least a week."

72
00:06:24.792 --> 00:06:28.854
"He can't play against the Bandits?" asked Patrick.

73
00:06:28.855 --> 00:06:34.697
Patrick had already started memorizing the Bandits' roster, the first team on the Dragons' regular schedule.

74
00:06:34.698 --> 00:06:41.109
"Nope." Dell looked grim. "And it will be a challenge to beat them without our star hitter."

75
00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:47.442
"You're right," Patrick agreed. "And . . ." His heart sank at another realization.

76
00:06:47.443 --> 00:06:52.407
"Mickey is a good hitter. Coach will probably start him as catcher."

77
00:06:52.408 --> 00:06:58.921
"Yep. In three weeks we play the Hornets—our biggest rivals. I hope Todd's back by then."

78
00:06:58.922 --> 00:07:03.068
Patrick nodded. He hoped Todd would be back by then too.

79
00:07:03.069 --> 00:07:07.660
The weather for practice after school was cold and dreary.

80
00:07:07.661 --> 00:07:12.411
Patrick worked with the fielders while Daniel spent extra time coaching Mickey.

81
00:07:12.412 --> 00:07:16.240
Patrick couldn't help glancing toward home plate a few times.

82
00:07:16.241 --> 00:07:21.493
"Way to go, Mickey!" Daniel kept saying. "You're framing pitches really well."

83
00:07:21.494 --> 00:07:26.410
Just then a ball thrown by the center fielder sailed past Patrick.

84
00:07:26.411 --> 00:07:32.814
"Patrick!" snapped Coach. "Are you picking dandelions out there? Where's your head?"

85
00:07:32.815 --> 00:07:38.900
"Sorry," muttered Patrick. He ran to retrieve the ball.

86
00:07:38.901 --> 00:07:41.868
"Pay attention!" he scolded himself.

87
00:07:41.869 --> 00:07:47.735
If he wasn't careful, he'd be sitting on the bench during games, with most of the other seventh-graders.

88
00:07:47.736 --> 00:07:56.124
Finally rain forced Coach to shorten practice. For once Patrick didn't mind going home early.

89
00:07:56.125 --> 00:08:08.997
He needed to study. His grade on the last math quiz had been better—but it wasn't good enough to satisfy his mother.
